[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have enough information. Let me create a comprehensive report:\n\n## Kynetic-Spec Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nI've conducted a thorough exploration of the kynetic-spec project structure, focusing on ralph command functionality, agent runtime systems, dispatch engine, and related test infrastructure. The codebase is well-organized with clear separation of concerns: CLI commands in `src/cli/commands/`, core agent/dispatch logic in `src/agent-runtime/`, and ralph-specific functionality in `src/ralph/`. Below is a detailed breakdown organized by area.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Ralph Command Structure (`src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`)\n\n**File Size:** ~2,250 lines of code\n\n**Key Exports & Subcommands:**\n- `registerRalphCommand(program)` - Main registration function\n- Two subcommands:\n  1. **`ralph end-loop`** - Signal to gracefully end the loop (lines 1265-1303)\n  2. **`ralph run`** (default) - Main execution with extensive options (lines 1306-2257)\n\n**Core Capabilities:**\n- Full loop orchestration with configurable iterations, retries, and failure handling\n- Per-role adapter support: `--worker-adapter` and `--reviewer-adapter` for task-work vs PR review\n- Explicit task scoping: `--tasks @ref1,@ref2` to limit work to specific tasks\n- Iteration timeout: `--iteration-timeout <minutes>` for safety\n- Session budget integration: `--max-tasks` creates `budget.json` for tracking\n- Streaming session updates with event logging\n- Terminal command execution with artifact capture\n- Subagent spawning for PR review tasks\n- Wrap-up agent on loop exit\n\n**Key Functions:**\n\n| Function | Purpose | Lines |\n|----------|---------|-------|\n| `parseExplicitTasks()` | Parse and validate `--tasks` flag (AC 21) | 110-143 |\n| `filterByExplicitTasks()` | Filter session context to explicit scope | 149-165 |\n| `buildTaskWorkPrompt()` | Build iteration prompt with focus & scope (AC 1-3) | 416-484 |\n| `buildReflectPrompt()` | Build post-task reflection prompt | 490-522 |\n| `runTerminalCommandWithArtifacts()` | Execute shell with bounded preview & artifact streaming | 676-779 |\n| `handleRequest()` | Tool request handler (file I/O, terminal, permissions) | 787-872 |\n| `processPendingReviewTasks()` | Spawn review subagents (AC 6-12) | 1116-1254 |\n| `handleIterationFailure()` | Track per-task failures with escalation (AC 1-8) | 1018-1110 |\n\n**Session Management:**\n- Creates session with `KSPEC_SESSION_ID` and `KSPEC_RALPH_SESSION` env vars\n- Uses `createSessionWithBudget()` when `--max-tasks` specified\n- Streams session updates to event log via `appendEvent()`\n- Cleans up budget via `removeEnvForAdapter()` on all exit paths\n- Signal handlers (SIGINT/SIGTERM) trigger graceful cleanup in finally block\n\n---\n\n## 2. Agent Command Family (`src/cli/commands/agent.ts`)\n\n**File Size:** ~680 lines\n\n**Subcommands:**\n\n| Command | Purpose | Lines |\n|---------|---------|-------|\n| `agent list` | List all agent definitions with filters | 81-209 |\n| `agent run` | One-shot invocation with task binding | 215-397 |\n| `agent status` | Show active & queued invocations (requires daemon) | 402-488 |\n| `agent dispatch start` | Start the dispatch engine | 498-552 |\n| `agent dispatch stop` | Stop dispatch gracefully | 555-604 |\n| `agent dispatch status` | Show engine status & loaded agents | 607-680 |\n\n**Key Features:**\n- List filtering: `--status eligible|ineligible`, `--tag`, pagination\n- One-shot run: `kspec agent run <agent-id> [prompt]` with `--task`, `--timeout`, `--budget` overrides\n- Dry-run support: shows prompt without spawning\n- JSON output for all commands\n- Daemon coordination via HTTP to localhost:3456 (configurable)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Agents Instruction Generation (`src/cli/commands/agents.ts`)\n\n**File Size:** ~510 lines\n\n**Subcommands:**\n\n| Command | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|\n| `agents generate` | Generate `kspec-agents.md` from meta + templates (AC 1-5) |\n| `agents status` | Check if file is current vs stale |\n\n**Key Functions:**\n- `loadTemplateSections()` - Load markdown templates in sorted order\n- `computeMetaHash()` - Hash meta for staleness detection (includes templates)\n- `generateAgentsContent()` - Compose final markdown from data + templates\n- `checkAgentStatus()` - Compare stored vs computed hashes\n\n**Freshness Tracking:**\n- Computes SHA256 hash of skills, conventions, workflows, templates\n- Stores hash & timestamp in `.kspec/.kspec-agents-hash`\n- Skips regeneration if content unchanged (optimization)\n\n---\n\n## 4. Ralph Module (`src/ralph/` directory)\n\n**6 files totaling ~60KB:**\n\n### `index.ts` (Exports Hub)\nRe-exports all ralph functionality:\n- CLI renderer & event translation\n- Subagent spawning & prompting\n- Loop error handling\n- Wrap-up agent\n\n### `cli-renderer.ts` (~9.3KB)\n- Translates ACP `SessionUpdate` events to `RalphEvent`\n- Renders events to console with formatting (thoughts, actions, tool results, status)\n- Supports custom prefixes for subagent output\n\n### `events.ts` (~24KB)\nCore event translation:\n- Maps ACP message types → `RalphEvent` types\n- Handles streaming text, tool calls, tool results\n- Translates thinking/action to structured events\n\n### `subagent.ts` (~14KB)\nPR review subagent spawning:\n- `runSubagent()` - Spawns agent with context, handles timeout, tracks result\n- `buildSubagentPrompt()` - Constructs prompt from task, spec, git context\n- `DEFAULT_SUBAGENT_TIMEOUT`: 20 minutes\n\n### `loop-errors.ts` (~5.2KB)\nFailure tracking & escalation:\n- `parseFailureCount()` - Parse `[LOOP-FAIL:N]` note prefix\n- `getTaskFailureCount()` - Get highest count from task notes\n- `processFailedIteration()` - Track failures per task\n- `shouldEscalate()` - Escalate to `automation:needs_review` at threshold (3 failures)\n\n### `wrap-up.ts` (~12.9KB)\nExit summary agent:\n- `runWrapUpAgent()` - Spawns final agent to summarize session\n- `buildWrapUpContext()` - Builds context from exit reason & pending tasks\n- Skips wrap-up for `dry_run` or certain exit reasons\n- Uses same adapter & auto-approve args as main worker\n\n---\n\n## 5. Agent Runtime / Dispatch (`src/agent-runtime/` directory)\n\n### `dispatch.ts` (~750 lines)\n\n**Core DispatchEngine Class:**\n\n**Constructor Options:**\n```typescript\ninterface DispatchEngineOptions {\n  projectDir: string;\n  specDir?: string;           // Defaults to .kspec/\n  cwd?: string;\n  dedupWindowMs?: number;     // Default 2000\n  kspecCliPath?: string;\n  onInvocationEvent?: (event: InvocationEvent) => void;\n}\n```\n\n**Public API:**\n\n| Method | Purpose | AC |\n|--------|---------|-----|\n| `start()` | Load tasks, bootstrap dispatch rules | ac-8 |\n| `handleStateChange()` | Process task state transitions | ac-1,2,4,5,6,7 |\n| `handleFileChange()` | Diff previous vs current task states | ac-5 |\n| `stop()` | Graceful shutdown with abort signals | ac-11 |\n| `getStatus()` | Return engine status + per-invocation details | ac-6 (CLI) |\n| `getShadowMutex()` | Get mutex for external serialization | ac-12 |\n\n**Key Features:**\n\n1. **State Change Matching (AC-1):**\n   - Maps task statuses → event types: `pending → task.ready`, `needs_work → task.needs_work`, `pending_review → task.pending_review`\n   - Matches against agent dispatch rules\n   - Each matching agent queued independently (AC-2)\n\n2. **Filter Evaluation (AC-6):**\n   - `automation`: \"eligible\" or \"ineligible\"\n   - `tags`: array of required tags\n   - `priority`: numeric priority level\n\n3. **Queuing & Concurrency (AC-3):**\n   - Per-agent queues\n   - Respects `agent.concurrency.max_concurrent`\n   - Drains queues after enqueuing\n\n4. **Deduplication (AC-7):**\n   - 2-second dedup window (configurable)\n   - Dedup key: `taskId:fromStatus:toStatus`\n   - Prunes expired entries periodically\n\n5. **Retry with Backoff (AC-9, AC-10):**\n   - Exponential backoff: 2^n seconds, capped at 30s\n   - Limit: `agent.budget.max_tasks` (default 3)\n   - Re-enqueues failed entries at front of queue\n\n6. **Graceful Shutdown (AC-11):**\n   - Sends AbortSignal to all active invocations\n   - Waits for all to complete\n\n7. **Shadow Mutation Serialization (AC-12):**\n   - All invocations wrapped in `shadowMutex`\n   - Prevents concurrent writes to shadow branch\n\n**Invocation Lifecycle (AC-9, AC-10, AC-11):**\n```\n1. Create AbortController\n2. Emit \"started\" event\n3. Call runInvocation() in mutex\n4. On success: emit \"completed\", reset retry count\n5. On error: emit \"failed\" or re-enqueue with backoff\n6. Finally: decrement active count, delete tracking records\n```\n\n### `invocation.ts` (~100 lines shown)\n\n**InvocationOptions:**\n```typescript\ninterface InvocationOptions {\n  agent: Agent;\n  specDir: string;\n  cwd: string;\n  taskRef?: string;           // @ref or @ulid\n  prompt: string;\n  trigger: SessionTrigger;    // \"dispatch\" | \"manual\" | \"schedule\"\n  timeoutMinutes?: number;    // Override agent.budget\n  autoApprove?: boolean;\n  env?: Record<string, string>;\n  onUpdate?: (update: SessionUpdate) => void;\n  kspecCliPath?: string;\n  abortSignal?: AbortSignal;\n  sessionId?: string;\n}\n```\n\n**Result:**\n```typescript\ninterface InvocationResult {\n  session: SessionMetadata;\n  outcome: \"success\" | \"timed_out\" | \"failed\";\n  stopReason?: string;\n  error?: string;\n  durationMs: number;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Agent Schema (`src/schema/meta.ts`)\n\n**Key Zod Schemas:**\n\n```typescript\n// Agent definition (AC: @agent-definition-schema ac-1 through ac-8)\nAgentSchema = z.object({\n  _ulid: MetaUlidSchema,\n  id: z.string(),             // \"task-worker\", \"pr-reviewer\"\n  name: z.string(),\n  description?: z.string(),\n  capabilities: z.array(z.string()),\n  tools: z.array(z.string()),\n  session_protocol?: SessionProtocolSchema,\n  conventions: z.array(z.string()),\n  \n  // Dispatch/runtime (NEW)\n  adapter?: z.string(),       // \"claude-agent-acp\" (default)\n  dispatch: z.array(AgentDispatchRuleSchema),\n  skills: z.array(z.string()),\n  budget?: AgentBudgetSchema,\n  concurrency: AgentConcurrencySchema,  // default { max_concurrent: 1 }\n  auto_approve: z.boolean(),  // For yolo mode\n  prompt_template?: z.string(),\n  automation?: \"eligible\" | \"ineligible\",\n  tags?: z.array(z.string()),\n});\n\n// Dispatch rule: maps event type + optional filters\nAgentDispatchRuleSchema = z.object({\n  on: z.enum([\"task.ready\", \"task.needs_work\", \"task.pending_review\"]),\n  filter?: AgentDispatchFilterSchema,\n});\n\n// Filter: narrowing constraints\nAgentDispatchFilterSchema = z.object({\n  automation?: \"eligible\" | \"ineligible\",\n  tags?: z.array(z.string()),\n  priority?: z.number(),\n});\n\n// Budget: task count and time limits\nAgentBudgetSchema = z.object({\n  max_tasks?: z.number().positive(),\n  timeout_minutes?: z.number().positive(),\n});\n\n// Concurrency: parallel limits\nAgentConcurrencySchema = z.object({\n  max_concurrent: z.number().int().positive(),  // default 1\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Parser / Meta Loading (`src/parser/meta.ts`)\n\n**LoadedAgent Interface:**\n```typescript\nexport interface LoadedAgent extends Agent {\n  // Inherits all Agent fields + resolved references\n}\n\nexport interface MetaContext {\n  agents: LoadedAgent[];\n  skills: LoadedSkill[];\n  conventions: LoadedConvention[];\n  workflows: LoadedWorkflow[];\n  // ... other meta items\n}\n```\n\n**Key Loading Functions:**\n- `loadMetaContext(ctx: KspecContext)` - Load all meta including agents\n- `loadAllTasks(ctx)` - Load task list with status, notes\n- `loadAllItems(ctx)` - Load all spec items\n\n---\n\n## 8. Test Structure\n\n### Test Files (`/tests/`):\n\n| Test File | Purpose | Key Tests |\n|-----------|---------|-----------|\n| `ralph.test.ts` (~150 lines) | Ralph command execution with mock ACP | Loop iterations, exit conditions, eligibility filtering, explicit task scope |\n| `ralph-loop-errors.test.ts` (~100 lines) | Error handling utilities | Failure count parsing, escalation thresholds, task progress detection |\n| `ralph-wrap-up.test.ts` | Wrap-up agent behavior | Exit reason handling, skip conditions |\n| `ralph-context-refresh.test.ts` | Context refresh after pending_review processing | Task state consistency |\n| `agent-dispatch-engine.test.ts` (~100 lines) | Core dispatch logic | State matching, filtering, queuing, deduplication, concurrency |\n| `agent-invocation-lifecycle.test.ts` | Invocation session creation/cleanup | Session tracking, timeout handling |\n| `cli-agent-commands.test.ts` | Agent CLI commands | List filtering, run overrides, dispatch engine control |\n| `agents-instruction-gen.test.ts` | kspec-agents.md generation | Template loading, hash staleness, dry-run |\n\n**Test Helpers in `tests/helpers/cli.ts`:**\n- `setupTempFixtures()` - Create temp dir with pre-built fixtures\n- `createTempDir()` - Empty temp directory\n- `initGitRepo(dir)` - Initialize git with test config\n- `testUlid(prefix?)` - Generate valid test ULIDs\n- `testUlids(prefix, count)` - Multiple unique ULIDs\n- `kspec(args, cwd)` - Run CLI command\n- `kspecJson<T>(args, cwd)` - Run CLI with `--json` parsing\n\n**Mock Fixtures:**\n- `tests/fixtures/mock-acp-agent.mjs` - Mock ACP agent for testing\n- `tests/fixtures/mock-acp-agent-crash.mjs` - Crashing variant\n- `tests/mocks/kspec-capture-mock.cjs` - Captures CLI calls for verification\n\n---\n\n## 9. Template File (`templates/agents-sections/06-ralph-loop.md`)\n\n**Content (~46 lines):**\n- Explains loop flow: task work → reflection → subagent review → iterate\n- Task inheritance priority: `needs_work > in_progress > pending`\n- Blocking rules: genuine blockers only (architectural decisions, spec clarifications, unavailable APIs, formal dependencies)\n- Auto-exit behavior: ralph exits when no tasks remain\n- Manual `end-loop` escape hatch (rare)\n\n---\n\n## 10. Architecture & Key Patterns\n\n### Session Management Flow:\n\n```\nkspec ralph run\n  ↓\ninitContext() → loadMetaContext() → load agents & skills\n  ↓\ncreateSessionWithBudget() → create session dir + budget.json\n  ↓\ninjectEnvForAdapter() → set KSPEC_SESSION_ID in harness config\n  ↓\nfor each iteration:\n  ├─ gatherSessionContext() → ready/active/pending_review tasks\n  ├─ processPendingReviewTasks() → spawn review subagent per task\n  ├─ spawnAndInitialize(workerAdapter) → create ACP agent\n  ├─ agent.client.newSession() → fresh ACP session per iteration\n  ├─ agent.client.prompt() → task-work phase\n  ├─ agent.client.prompt() → reflect phase\n  ├─ check for iteration timeout\n  └─ on failure: handleIterationFailure() → track per-task\n  ├─ runWrapUpAgent() → exit summary\n  └─ closeSession() + removeEnvForAdapter() → cleanup\n```\n\n### Dispatch Engine Flow:\n\n```\nDispatchEngine.start()\n  ↓\n_bootstrap() → evaluate all current tasks against rules\n  ↓\nExternal event: handleStateChange() | handleFileChange()\n  ↓\n_matchesFilter() → check automation, tags, priority\n  ↓\n_enqueue() → per-agent queue\n  ↓\n_drainQueues() → spawn up to max_concurrent per agent\n  ↓\n_spawnInvocation() → runInvocation() in shadowMutex\n  ↓\nretry on error (AC-9, AC-10)\n```\n\n### Skill Invocation Resolution:\n\n```\nresolveRalphSkillInvocation(invocation, platform, skillOrigins)\n  ↓\ntokenResolved = resolveSkillReferenceTokensForPlatform()\n  └─ {skill:id} → /kspec:id (claude-code) or $kspec-id (codex)\n  ↓\nnormalizeLegacyInvocation() → backward compat\n  └─ /kspec:foo ↔ $kspec-foo per platform\n```\n\n---\n\n## 11. Key Acceptance Criteria Coverage\n\n**Ralph Loop (AC @cli-ralph):**\n- AC-1: Basic loop execution\n- AC-2: Exit when no ready tasks\n- AC-14: Fresh ACP session per iteration\n- AC-16: Only automation-eligible tasks\n- AC-17: Periodic agent restart\n- AC-19: Check for active/ready tasks\n- AC-20: Context refresh after pending_review\n- AC-21: Explicit task scope with `--tasks`\n\n**Dispatch Engine (AC @agent-dispatch-engine):**\n- AC-1: Match against dispatch rules\n- AC-2: Each matching agent queued independently\n- AC-3: Enqueue + drain respecting concurrency\n- AC-4: N/A (per spec)\n- AC-5: File watcher diffing\n- AC-6: Filter evaluation (automation, tags, priority)\n- AC-7: Deduplication with window\n- AC-8: Bootstrap evaluation\n- AC-9, AC-10: Retry with backoff + adapter validation\n- AC-11: Graceful shutdown with abort signals\n- AC-12: Mutex serialization for shadow mutations\n\n**Agent Definition Schema (AC @agent-definition-schema):**\n- AC-1-8: Full agent schema with dispatch rules, budget, concurrency, automation, tags\n\n---\n\n## 12. Summary: What Code Already Exists\n\n**Complete & Production-Ready:**\n1. ✅ Ralph command with full loop orchestration\n2. ✅ Per-role adapter support (worker + reviewer)\n3. ✅ Explicit task scoping (`--tasks`)\n4. ✅ Dispatch engine with rule matching, filtering, concurrency\n5. ✅ Agent schema with dispatch rules, budget, concurrency\n6. ✅ Session management with budget tracking\n7. ✅ Error handling with per-task failure tracking\n8. ✅ Wrap-up agent on loop exit\n9. ✅ Agent instruction generation from meta + templates\n10. ✅ Comprehensive test coverage (dispatch, ralph, invocation, instructions)\n\n**Key File Locations:**\n- Ralph: `/src/cli/commands/ralph.ts`\n- Dispatch: `/src/agent-runtime/dispatch.ts`\n- Invocation: `/src/agent-runtime/invocation.ts`\n- Agent schema: `/src/schema/meta.ts`\n- Ralph utils: `/src/ralph/` (6 files)\n- Tests: `/tests/` (13+ test files)\n- Templates: `/templates/agents-sections/`\n\n---\n\nThis exploration provides a complete map of the codebase structure for migration planning. The architecture is well-established, thoroughly tested, and ready for agent dispatch feature development."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: acdea03 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 96363\ntool_uses: 22\nduration_ms: 69624</usage>"}]